\Q\You're outside of the Beatles' hotel.  There are thousands of other
fans waiting at the front entrance.  What do you do?
\A\Wait with everyone else.
\A\Walk in and get a room.
\A\Look around the building.
\N\You and the other fans waited for hours but never did see
even one Beatle.  You caught a cold and ended up in the hospital.
\N\"There are no vacancies!  Now get out of here!",
the manager shouted.
\Y\You wonder down an alley beside the building...

\Q\Near the back of the building, you spot not only an
unlocked door but also an open window.
\A\Slip through the door.
\A\Climb through the window.
\A\Go inform the hotel manager that his security isn't very good.
\N\As you entered the dark room you noticed a strange smell...
GARBAGE!  You turned to leave but someone shut the door and
locked it.
\Y\You find that you are now in the laundry room.
\N\"You Beatlemaniacs think you own this place!
GUARD!  Call the police."

\Q\You approach the door cautiously and look out into the hallway.
You decide to:
\A\Dress up in the maid's uniform.
\A\Hide in a laundry cart.
\A\Walk down the hall.
\N\You walked past the security guards with no problem and headed
for the elevator.  The hotel manager got on the elevator with you
and somewhere around the 4th floor he figured out that you had
on the wrong type of shoes.  "My maids only wear WHITE shoes!",
he shouted.  He took you back downstairs and tossed you out the
front door.
\N\Just as you covered yourself up with the towels and pillowcases,
you heard someone enter the room.  They started pushing the cart,
with you in it, down the hallway.  After a couple of minutes they
stopped.
 
Then there was a little bouncing around.
 
Then you heard a motor start and a truck from the local laundry
drove you and the dirty laundry across town where you spent the
day in a washing machine.
\Y\You walk down the hallway quietly.

\Q\Halfway down the hall you find two doors.  You should:
\A\Open the door labeled "Kitchen"
\A\Open the door labeled "Stairs"
\A\Continue down the hall
\Y\There's no one in the room.
\N\You started up the stairs...
And climbed...
And climbed...
At the 4th floor you encountered a guard who shook his head
and said "Not another one!"  You were escourted to the front
door and returned to the large crowd of screaming fans.
\N\You walked another 10 feet and suddenly the hotel manager
appeared from around the corner.  "GUARD!", he called.  You
were then taken to the nearest exit and ordered to leave.

\Q\You look around and wonder if any of the food is for the Beatles.
You hear someone coming and...
\A\Hide under the nearest dinner cart.
\A\Hide in the closet.
\A\Hide in the refrigerator.
\Y\Someone enters the room and starts pushing the cart you're
hiding under.
\N\The janitor locked the closet and you missed The Beatles
when they dropped by to sneak a snack from the kitchen.
\N\Bad move!  You weren't found until the next Christmas when
the cook decided to defrost a turkey.

\Q\You and the cart are rolled onto an elevator.  A hotel guest
is also on the elevator with her dog.  The dog starts growling
at the cart.
\A\You growl back.
\A\You sit silently.
\A\You hiss like a cat.
\Y\The dog backs off and no one else heard you.
\N\The dog jumped under the table cloth and exposed you.
You were tossed out the nearest door.
\N\The dog bit you and you caught rabies and died a horrible death.

\Q\The elevator stops and the waiter pushes the cart into the hallway.
He leaves you and the cart for a moment as he sneaks into a closet
with the maid.  You decide to...
\A\Join the waiter and maid in the closet.
\A\Sneak down the hall.
\A\Wait on the waiter to return.
\N\The maid's husband, who happened to be the hotel security guard,
caught the three of you in the closet and started firing his pistol
without asking questions.
\N\You ran into Brian Epstein, The Beatles' manager, who said
"Hello, chap." and then had you removed from the hotel.
\Y\The waiter returns and pushes the cart down the hall.

\Q\Soon you reach a room.  The waiter knocks, someone opens the
door, and the cart is pulled into the room.  You decide to:
\A\Peek out from under the table cloth.
\A\Hop out and hope for the best.
\A\Wait and hope you hear English accents.
\N\You saw The Beatles' manager and he saw you.  Within a few
moments you were back out on the street with all of the other fans.
\N\You hopped out and caught the waiter with another maid.  One
broken nose later, you were back out front with a million other fans.
\Y\At first you hear a reporter asking questions about barbers.

\Q\Then you hear a man with an English accent!  You decide to:
\A\Hop out and pray that it's not a famous English hairstylist.
\A\Wait for someone to ask about The Beatles record company, Apple
Records.
\W\You jumped out and came face to face with John, Paul, George and
Ringo!
\N\Since The Beatles didn't start Apple Records for several more
years, you had a very long and useless wait.

\END\


